{"uncertainty": 0.35, "outcome": "Wrote a self-checking SystemVerilog testbench, tick_timer_cov_tb.sv, that extends the approved idle testbench. It runs one-shot and periodic counting, expiry with and without the interrupt, write-one-to-clear, expiry winning over a same-edge clear, a CTRL write suppressing an expiry, stop with no restart, reads of all four registers, all-ones and all-zeros traffic on every stored bit, and a reset mid-run. Wrote a coverage report covering intended reach and points the design cannot toggle. No coverage numbers are reported because no coverage run has happened yet.", "artifacts": [{"kind": "coverage_report", "title": "tick_timer coverage plan and expected gaps (pre-run)", "summary": "This is analysis of the approved RTL [artifact:prj-4fd2403e98.design-under-test.a1] for [requirement:req-33bb46282b]. It is not a measurement. The approved idle testbench [artifact:prj-4fd2403e98.testbench.a1] passed 5 checks [evidence:prj-4fd2403e98.testbench.e1], but its own header says it never starts the timer, so its coverage stays below bounds. The new testbench is aimed at every line and branch: reset, LOAD write, a CTRL write with start, a CTRL write without start, decrement, periodic reload, one-shot stop, and all four rdata cases. It also aims to toggle both edges of every bit of clk, rst_n, we, addr, wdata[31:0], rdata[15:0], irq, en, mode, ie, load, count, expired, wr_ctrl, wr_status and expire. Two kinds of toggle point cannot be reached at W=16, and both are structural, not stimulus gaps. First, rdata[31:16] is always zero, because the always block assigns only rdata[W-1:0]. Second, unused_wdata is the constant AND of 1'b0 with other bits, so it is always 0. I did not change the parameter to hide these points. Toggle coverage therefore cannot reach 100 percent. Whether it meets the requirement's bound depends on bounds not given to me. Actual line, toggle and branch percentages must come from the platform's coverage.read run over this testbench."}], "files": [{"path": "tick_timer_cov_tb.sv", "kind": "testbench", "title": "tick_timer_cov_tb.sv: coverage-closing self-checking testbench", "summary": "This testbench extends the approved idle testbench [artifact:prj-4fd2403e98.testbench.a1] against the approved RTL [artifact:prj-4fd2403e98.design-under-test.a1], serving [requirement:req-33bb46282b]. It instantiates tick_timer with W=16. Its checks are cycle-exact and derived from the RTL's next-state logic, and they cover: reset values; LOAD readback; one-shot count 3 down to 0, then expiry with irq and EN cleared; a W1C write of 0 (no effect) and of 1 (clears); a periodic reload over two periods; expiry winning over a same-edge clear; a CTRL write suppressing expiry; stop with no decrement; LOAD 0xFFFFFFFF reading as 0x0000FFFF; a restart from LOAD 0; and a reset mid-run. It prints the NIRMAAN-SIM verdict line with the plusarg nonce. It uses no $fopen, $system, DPI, include or coverage pragmas.", "entry": "tick_timer_cov_tb"}], "tool_runs": [], "claims": ["Expected cycle timing (for example, expiry 4 edges after a start with LOAD=3) is derived by hand from the RTL. It has not been simulated.", "rdata[31:16] and unused_wdata are expected to be untoggleable at W=16, by inspection of the RTL.", "The testbench is expected to build under Verilator with timing enabled, but this has not been checked."], "escalation": null, "notes": "No coverage bounds were given. If the toggle bound requires every bit, it cannot be met at W=16, because of the structural points named above. In that case the bound or an exclusion would need a decision from verification.dynamic.coverage.code.senior. I did not use coverage pragmas or parameter changes to hide those points. run-0001 belongs to the earlier idle testbench, so it is not listed as a run of this work."}
